MODULE <option> [argument]

Manages modules on the local server.

  LIST [pattern]       Lists names, states and protection flags.
                       Supports * and ? wildcards.
  LOAD <module_name>   Loads a configured module not already listed.
  UNLOAD <module_name> Unloads an active module or removes a failed entry.
  RELOAD <module_name> Reloads an active module or retries a failed entry.
  RELOAD *             Reloads listed modules, skipping unconfigured
                       modules and protected active modules. Stops at
                       the first error.

Names are case-sensitive; omit paths and .so suffixes.
LOAD and RELOAD require a current configuration entry.

Protection flags:
  no_remove     - Blocks UNLOAD.
  no_deactivate - Blocks UNLOAD and RELOAD of active modules.

Modules in state broken are quarantined and require a server restart.
A failed reload may leave a module inactive. The server terminates if
any required module is inactive.

MODULE does not change configuration. REHASH CONF may reactivate
unloaded modules that remain configured.

- Requires Oper Priv: module
